<title>GERMANY: Alcatel German unit narrows Q1 loss.</title>
<headline>Alcatel German unit narrows Q1 loss.</headline>
<dateline>STUTTGART, Germany 1997-06-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Alcatel SEL AG, a German electronics unit of French industrial group Alcatel Alsthom said on Thursday that a 28 percent rise in first quarter sales to 957 million marks helped narrow its operating loss in the quarter compared to the same period a year ago.</p>
<p>The first-quarter operating loss was  103.9 million marks, down from 323.8 million in the first three months of 1996. The unit expected rising sales would produce a &quot;clearly positive&quot; result for all of 1997.</p>
<p>The company had a 1996 loss on ordinary activities of 589.6 million marks, and had begun restructuring to improve results.</p>
<p>-- Bonn Newsroom, +49-228 26097150</p>
</text>
